<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n83390" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλᾰγι-άζω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλάγιος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>turn
			sideways</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ἵππον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					1.204
				</span></i>
			 ; in wrestling, <i>throw sideways</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.155
			</span></i> ; of ships, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. πρὸς ἀντίους τοὺς
				ἐτησίας</span>
			<i>sail athwart</i> the trade-winds, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Nav.</u>
				9
			</span></i>; dub. sens. in <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				5.88
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>hold aslant</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάτοπτρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ach.Tat.
					<u>Intr.Arat.</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλαγιαζέσθω τὰ
			τρήματα</span> let the holes <i>be made obliquely</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
				<u>Poliorc.</u>
				151.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύλινδρος ἀπὸ τῆς ὀρθότητος -ασθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hierocl.
					<u>in CA</u>
					24p.474M.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>lead astray</i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ez.</u>
				14.5
			</span></i> ; <i>pervert</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ἀδίκοις
				δίκαιον</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Is.</u>
				29.21
			</span></i> : abs., <i>use tortuous methods</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. καὶ τεχνιτεύειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.432
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἢ φωνὴν ἢ πρᾶξιν</span>
			in word or deed, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Dem.</u>
				13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>strike with the flat of the sword</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				40.53
			</span></i>(
				Pass.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> Gramm.,
				<i>inflect, decline</i>, Sch.rec.<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				365
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεπλαγίασται ὁ λόγος</span>,
			of Tragic irony, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				137
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1183
			</span></i>.</div>
